    }
  ],
  "permissions": [
    {
      "runtime": "codex",
      "files": [
        ".codex/config.toml",
        ".codex/rules/gstack-adapted.rules"
      ],
      "effect": "Keeps the Codex sandbox ON (no general network). The checker can write in the project and the system's temporary folders. OpenRig also lists one more folder in the seat's sandbox policy, <OpenRig shared-docs root>/rigs/<rig>/state/<pod>, but does not create it and this factory does not use it; writes there fail unless something else has created it. One command runs outside the sandbox without a prompt: `rig …`. Codex runs a command line outside the sandbox only when EVERY command in it is allowed, so `rig` chained with any other command runs inside the sandbox and fails; run `rig` on its own, one per call. Reading the diff, running the CLI directly and writing the report work inside the sandbox; tests that start child processes do not: they fail with EPERM or hang until a timeout, so the checker probes behaviour directly and asks the builder for the suite's result. Codex loads these only for a trusted project; launching with OpenRig registers that trust.",
      "tested": "gstack-adapted 0.1.2 author proof and 0.1.3 independent QA from the download (OpenRig 0.6.1, Codex 0.159.0, 2026-09-29): the checker's standalone rig calls handed work on; git reads, direct CLI probes and report writing ran inside the sandbox; a test suite starting child processes failed with EPERM or hung. The rules and config are unchanged in behaviour since (0.1.4 changes a comment only)."
    },
    {
      "runtime": "claude-code",
      "files": [
        ".claude/settings.json"
      ],
      "effect": "Pre-approves only `rig`, `node --test`, `node example-cli/bin/wordstat.mjs`, the git commands the builder needs to set up and commit (`git init`, `status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`, `add`, `commit`, and the repository-local `git config user.name` / `git config user.email`), `mkdir` and `ls`. `git config --global` is not approved. No general shell and no `git push`; anything else asks as usual.",
      "tested": "gstack-adapted 0.1.2 author proof and 0.1.3 independent QA from the download (OpenRig 0.6.1, Claude Code 2.1.220, 2026-09-29): the builder ran git init and the repository-local git config user.name/user.email without a prompt; no seat stopped at a permission prompt. The settings file is unchanged since 0.1.2."
    }
  ],
